hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1743","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam, he said: My father and Shu'ayb narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid—he is Ibn Yazid—from Ibn Abi Hilal—he is Sa'id—from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, that 'Amr ibn Sulaym informed him, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Indeed"," the bath on the day of Friday is obligatory upon every post-pubescent person"," and the use of the tooth-stick"," and that one should apply some perfume if he is able to.\"""""
"1744","**\nNarrated to us Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzar: Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' Abu 'Amr ibn al-Basri: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from 'Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Ghusl (ritual bath) on the day of Jumu'ah (Friday) is obligatory upon every post-pubescent person"," and let him apply perfume if he has any.\"""""
"1745","**\nNarrated to us Abu Yahya, he said: narrated to us Ali ibn Abdullah, he said: narrated to us Harami ibn Umarah, he said: narrated to us Shu'bah, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, who said: 'Amr ibn Sulaym narrated to me, he said: I bear witness over Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (RA), that he bore witness over the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said:\n\n*\The bath on Friday is obligatory upon every post-pubescent person"," as is using the tooth-stick and applying perfume if available.\""*\n\n'Amr said: As for the bath"," I bear witness that it is obligatory. As for the tooth-stick"," Allah knows best whether it is obligatory or not"," but this is how it was narrated."""
"1746","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-'Attar, the Persian by origin who resided in al-Fustat, who said: Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah, who said: Narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n*\The Friday bath is obligatory upon every post-pubescent person.\""*\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said: I do not deny that Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir may have heard from Jabir (RA) the mention of the obligation of the bath upon the post-pubescent person without the use of perfume or brushing the teeth.\n\nIt was also narrated from his brother Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir"," on the authority of 'Amr ibn Sulaym"," on the authority of Abu Sa'id (RA)"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," the obligation of the bath and the use of perfume if available. This is because Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from Abu Zubayr"," on the authority of Jabir (RA)"," from the Prophet (ﷺ):\n\n*\""Upon every Muslim man"," it is obligatory to perform a bath once every seven days"," and that day is Friday.\""*"""
"1747","**\nNarrated to us Bundar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Dawud; and narrated to us Abu al-Khattab, narrated to us Bishr (meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal), narrated to us Dawud. Also, narrated to us Bundar, narrated to us 'Abd al-Wahhab, from Dawud.\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said: In this narration, the Prophet (ﷺ) has combined the use of the siwak (tooth-stick) and applying perfume with the Friday bath. He (ﷺ) informed that these are for every post-pubescent person. The siwak purifies the mouth, and perfume beautifies the body, removing offensive odors from it.\n\nWe have not heard any Muslim claim that using the siwak on Friday or applying perfume is an obligation (fard), nor is the bath itself obligatory in the same manner. Rather, evidence from other chapters—if Allah wills—indicates that the Friday bath is not an obligation, and nothing else suffices in its place."
